# ==============================================================================
# Panic Alarm Server — System Configuration Properties (server.env)
#
# Clinic IT Administrators can edit this file to configure network ports,
# IP bindings, and database storage paths.
#
# To apply: rename this file to "server.env" and place it next to the
# installed application executable before launching.
# ==============================================================================

# Network Port the server listens on.
# If left commented out (or set to 0), the server automatically picks the next
# free port on the machine and displays it on the login screen at startup.
# Only set this if you need a fixed port (e.g. for firewall rules).
# PORT=<port-number>

# Host network interface to bind to.
# - Use 0.0.0.0 to allow client apps on other network computers to connect.
# - Use 127.0.0.1 to lock all incoming traffic to localhost only.
# Defaults to 0.0.0.0 if not set.
# HOST=<ip-or-0.0.0.0>

# Path to the SQLite database file.
# If left commented out, the server stores the database in the secure
# OS-specific AppData directory so updates never overwrite your data.
# DB_PATH=<absolute-or-relative-path-to-database-file>

# ==============================================================================
# E-mail alerts (SMTP)
#
# With these set, EVERY panic alarm is e-mailed with its full details (who sent it, from which room,
# every receiving station and whether it was delivered) to the clinic's contact e-mail
# (Add/Edit Client -> Email) and to ALARM_EMAIL_TO below. The alarm logs can also be e-mailed
# from the admin panel (Alarm Logs -> Email).
#
# TLS 1.2 or higher is always required and the mail server's certificate is always verified.
# Keep the real values ONLY in server.env on the server PC — never commit them.
# ==============================================================================
# SMTP_HOST=<mail-server-host-name>
# SMTP_PORT=587                 # 587 = STARTTLS (default), 465 = TLS from the start
# SMTP_SECURE=false             # true for port 465
# SMTP_USER=<smtp-login-user>   # leave out if your relay needs no login
# SMTP_PASS=<smtp-login-password>
# SMTP_FROM=<Panic Alarm <alerts@your-hospital.org>>
# Extra address(es) that receive every alarm, besides each clinic's own contact e-mail (comma separated)
# ALARM_EMAIL_TO=<security@your-hospital.org>
